Looking at the failures, the issue is timing of `doneSensor` confirmation. In `fill-limit-2`, after accumulating reaches target (valve closes in same scan), the test expects fillsToday=32767 in that same scan because doneSensor is already TRUE. But my code defers the confirmation check to the next scan (state=2).

The fix: when accumulated reaches targetVol in state=1, check doneSensor immediately in the same scan. If TRUE, increment count and go to idle. If FALSE, go to pendingConfirm state.

```json
{"edits":[{"old": "        1: // filling
            tmp_accVol := tmp_accVol + flowVol;
            IF tmp_accVol >= targetVol THEN
                valveOpen := FALSE;
                tmp_pending := TRUE;
                state := 2;
            END_IF;", "new": "        1: // filling
            tmp_accVol := tmp_accVol + flowVol;
            IF tmp_accVol >= targetVol THEN
                valveOpen := FALSE;
                IF doneSensor THEN
                    IF fillsToday < 32767 THEN
                        fillsToday := fillsToday + 1;
                    END_IF;
                    tmp_pending := FALSE;
                    state := 0;
                ELSE
                    tmp_pending := TRUE;
                    state := 2;
                END_IF;
            END_IF;"}]}
```
